    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d466">

                <pb facs="0395" n="383" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg383"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/22468: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hibbard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-27T19:00:00-04:00">June 27, 1942—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>173. Your 211, June 25, 4 p.m. You may deliver the following message to President
                    Barclay from President Roosevelt: <pb facs="0396" n="384" xml:id="pg384"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I am gratified at the signing of an agreement which binds our two
                            countries together in the common purpose of resisting the forces of
                            aggression. As a practical matter, I hope that for the present no
                            publicity will be given to Liberia’s courageous action.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
